			"Message": "style(Mountain): Clean up formatting across ApplicationState modules and command handlers\n\nApply consistent formatting improvements across Mountain's application state hierarchy, command registration, document save operations, workspace provider, extension scanner, and shutdown logic:\n\n- Convert multi-line `use std::{...}` imports to single-line format across 20+ state modules (ConfigurationState, ExtensionRegistry, ProviderRegistration, ScannedExtensions, DebugState, DecorationsState, DiagnosticsState, DocumentState, KeybindingState, LifecyclePhaseState, MarkerState, NavigationHistoryState, OutputChannelState, TreeViewState, WebviewState, WorkingCopyState, UIState, WorkspaceState)\n- Condense single-statement getter methods to single-line format (GetAll, Get, Count, Contains variants)\n- Normalize lock acquisition patterns: remove extra blank lines around `.lock()` calls, standardize guard binding\n- Fix indentation in AppLifecycle (GlobalMementoPath setup), Entry (dev_log call), Bootstrap command registration, FileExplorerViewProvider\n- Simplify SCM command handlers (GetAllSourceControlManagementState, GetSCMResourceChanges) by inlining lock/clone chains\n- Clean up DocumentProvider save operations: flatten nested lock access paths\n- Fix WorkspaceProvider walk loop indentation (break/quit conditions)\n- Update ExtensionManagement scanner and default configs: flatten Extensions lock access\n- Add missing newlines at end of files (ApplicationState.rs, ConfigurationState.rs, ExtensionRegistry.rs, ProviderRegistration.rs, ScannedExtensions.rs, DebugState.rs, DecorationsState.rs, DiagnosticsState.rs, DocumentState.rs, KeybindingState.rs, LifecyclePhaseState.rs, MarkerState.rs, NavigationHistoryState.rs, OutputChannelState.rs, TreeViewState.rs, WebviewState.rs, WorkingCopyState.rs, UIState.rs, WorkspaceState.rs, SaveApplicationState.rs, VineHostImpl.rs)\n- Fix shell integration script: add space in `2> /dev/null` redirection\n\nNo functional changes — purely mechanical formatting cleanup for consistency across Mountain's state management layer and related command handlers.",
			"SHA": "a94d949e10d5ba5d46a408ff3c7ef99d2dc6f684"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-05T10:35:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1731,
				35
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Complete parking_lot migration for ApplicationState and command modules\n\nMigrate the remaining std::sync::Mutex and tokio::sync::RwLock usage in Mountain's ApplicationState hierarchy to parking_lot equivalents. This completes the migration started in the previous commit, covering all feature state modules (Debug, Decorations, Diagnostics, Documents, Keybindings, LifecyclePhase, Markers, NavigationHistory, OutputChannels, TreeViews, Webviews, WorkingCopy), UI state, workspace state, configuration state, and extension registry.\n\nKey changes:\n- Replace Arc<StandardMutex<>> and Arc<tokio::sync::RwLock<>> with Arc<parking_lot::Mutex<>> and Arc<parking_lot::RwLock<>> across 20+ state modules\n- Remove MapLockError/MapLockErrorWithRecovery helpers and StateOperationResult — parking_lot panics on poison instead of returning Result, eliminating poison-error boilerplate\n- Simplify lock acquisition from guard.ok().and_then(|g| g.clone()) to direct .lock().clone() patterns\n- Update command handlers (Bootstrap, SCM commands), document save operations, extension scanner, file explorer, and shutdown logic to use the new locking API\n- Remove ErrorMapping crate's PoisonError mapping functions (now replaced by WithParkingLotMutex helper)\n- Fix VineHostImpl.UpdateScmGroupMarkers lock handling\n\nImpact: Consistent parking_lot usage across Mountain's entire state management layer, reduced lock contention overhead, and cleaner error handling paths without .ok().and_then() chains.",
			"SHA": "6a285173d703deccb702306a329811b0b9e0f448"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-05T08:40:06Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1731,
				11
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Migrate std::sync::Mutex to parking_lot::Mutex and modernize lazy static initialization\n\nReplace standard library mutexes with parking_lot::Mutex across terminal state management, IPC connection pools, secure message channels, performance dashboard, and Cocoon process management. The parking_lot implementation provides faster lock acquisition and doesn't return Result from lock() (panics on poison instead), simplifying error handling throughout the codebase.\n\nSimultaneously replace lazy_static macros with once_cell::sync::Lazy for global registry initialization (feature flags, metrics, Cocoon state), adopting the more modern and maintenance-friendly pattern.\n\nKey changes:\n- TerminalState and TerminalStateDTO: Arc<Mutex<>> replaces Arc<StandardMutex<>> for PTY handles and terminal collections\n- TerminalProvider: Output buffer and terminal map locks simplified; removed MapLockErrorToCommonError mappings\n- ErrorMapping: Added WithParkingLotMutex helper for the new locking pattern\n- IPC Enhanced modules: ConnectionPool, MessageCompressor, PerformanceDashboard, SecureMessageChannel all updated\n- CocoonManagement: lazy_static replaced with once_cell::Lazy for COCOON_STATE and COCOON_HEALTH\n- Telemetry registries: FeatureFlags and Metrics global registries migrated to once_cell::Lazy\n- Vine client/server notification shims: Minor formatting normalization\n\nImpact: Reduced lock contention overhead, cleaner error handling paths (no more .ok().and_then() chains for mutex access), and modernized static initialization across Mountain's core subsystems.",
			"SHA": "3b0c95e2986ddeebe6dfa24f4e7a1652a0d5d670"
		},
